Hi [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] ,

Thank you for your prompt responses!

{quote}* Good news is that this support will be classified as no risk AI system under the EU AI Act, it means we have no additional requirements, apart from the privacy law.{quote}

Yay! 

{quote}You stated that “This led us to considering Gemini assistance within Google sheets first” - does it mean you will copy the CS ticket content to a Google sheet → send to Gemini for  analysis → resolve a case in Beehive?{quote}

The plan is to extract the data in the following format
0: {"first text message"}
1: {"reply text message 1"}
2: {"reply text message 2"}
and so on for each conversation / case. 


Next - put it into Google Sheet, ask Gemini to extract specific pattern from each case, count the number of cases, where a pattern occurred. 

We (Insights) have nothing to do with the actual case resolution in Beehive, we analyse aggregated data and report the insights to Ops, Product or CS stakeholders. We are not interested in individual cases or customers, *we report results from the aggregated data*. 

{quote}* This is a concern as we will duplicate CS tickets into G Drive where we have no centralised retention periods. It means data of our users will be scattered around G Drive that should not be the case.
* The only proposal is to use it as a temporary measure - 1-2 months to understand whether API is reasonable and have a use case to request API.
* Once 1-2 months passed, delete the data copied to G Drive{quote}

I hear you, clear. We can even delete it within several days after the analysis is completed. We have no interest in this data beyond the insights. 

{quote}We would need to ensure that:

* Analysis of the tickets is correct and not biased{quote}

That is our goal as well! If the analysis is biased it has no value at all. 

{quote}* If it translates from X language to English, we need to ensure the translation is correct.{quote}

I think we will use the originals for Gemini. 

{quote}* There should be human involvement before response and support is provided{quote}

*We are data analysts, we do interact directly with the customers at all.* 

{quote}* Privacy requests (we can provide specific issues tags) must be approved with our team once the test is done to ensure the summarisation works correctly.{quote}

Yes, please, if you could provide the issue tags, that would be great. Thank you! We will keep an eye on them if we plan any analysis for such tickets. At the moment we do not have such plans.  

{quote}* Do you have a specific RFC for this project?{quote}

No, we do not, there is no point to create a documentation if the legal side is not understood well. Besides, we need to make a few experiments first before creating any project suggestion, to understand what is doable. 

There is also a huge need to make the analysis of customer experience tickets more efficient and less manual, and a firm push from the management.

